Part B: Introduction to EDA

19. What is EDA?

EDA (Exploratory Data Analysis) is the process of understanding, cleaning, analyzing, and visualizing data before applying Machine Learning models.

Why EDA?

Understand data

Find missing values

Detect outliers

Identify patterns

Make better decisions



---

20. EDA vs Python Programming

Python Programming	EDA

Used to write programs	Used to analyze data
Focus on coding	Focus on data insights
Uses loops and functions	Uses statistics and visualization
Builds applications	Finds patterns and trends


Case Study

Suppose a school has student marks.

Python Programming

Calculates total marks.

Prints pass/fail.


EDA

Finds average marks.

Detects highest and lowest marks.

Identifies missing values.

Creates charts to analyze performance.



