Exam Summary

NumPy is a fast numerical computing library used for arrays.

Use indexing, slicing, Boolean indexing, reshape(), ravel(), flatten(), and transpose() for array manipulation.

Combine arrays using concatenate(), vstack(), hstack(), column_stack(), hsplit(), and vsplit().

Sort arrays using sort() and argsort().

Broadcasting and vectorization make array operations faster without loops.

NumPy provides mathematical functions (sqrt, exp, sin, cos, dot) and statistical functions (mean, median, var, std, corrcoef).

EDA (Exploratory Data Analysis) is the process of understanding and analyzing data before building Machine Learning models.

Statistics helps summarize and interpret data using measures of central tendency (mean, median, mode) and dispersion (range, variance, standard deviation).